  "notes": "Event date on FORM-366 (2024-09-27) conflicts with narrative Safety Analysis section which states 'October 27, 2024' for the 07:48 EDT event time; treated as a narrative typo and FORM-366 date retained as authoritative per instructions, while the 07:48 EDT time from the narrative was used for the Consequence timestamp. Plant/unit/reactor type inferred from title and narrative (Catawba is a Westinghouse PWR) since identity fields were null in FORM-366. The Unit 1 AFW loss-of-safety-function initially reported in EN 57344 was later determined NOT reportable/not a loss of safety function after further review, so no FailureMode/Consequence node was created for it, per rule 1 (avoid creating entities not part of the confirmed event) -- only the confirmed Unit 2 RPS/AFW actuation and Unit 1 power reduction are modeled. No previous similar LER was cited (explicitly stated none in last three years), so no stub LER/SIMILAR_TO edge emitted per rule 9's implicit requirement of an actual reference by the narrative."
